{"name":"Malaysia","slug":"malaysia","code":"MY","continent":"Asia","hero":"plonkit/malaysia/pexels-zukiman-mohamad-125486.webp","updated":"2026-07-20T17:57:14.943Z","sections":[{"title":"Identifying Malaysia","title_zh":"辨識馬來西亞","items":[{"id":"r0EY","text":["Malaysian licence plates are **black** and generally have **two** white sections. These are visible even when blurred.","NOTE: Indonesian licence plates can also be black, but they will have **three** white sections."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Malaysia_License_Plate.webp","link":"","clues":["license_plates"],"important":false,"tagged":true},{"id":"5Y5B","text":["Malaysia frequently uses **double white** centre lines on its two-lane roads. It is the only Southeast Asian country to do so."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Road_lines.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/xnmKE1q4Nz91xA528","clues":["lines"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"FTvY","text":["These **thick yellow bars** are also almost exclusive to Malaysia.","NOTE: You can very rarely see similar patterns in [Hong Kong](https://maps.app.goo.gl/PSUAhJVM8bCQUhH36) and the [United Kingdom](https://maps.app.goo.gl/BKn4346rfTwJj3L26)."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/yellow_road_markings.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/CC7S8r8KEEYHF1yY8","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"Dwit","text":["Electricity poles in Malaysia often have **black** or **white** stickers on them.","Sometimes you will also find red-and-white or red-and-blue stripes below the black sticker."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Untitled_design__2825_29.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/FR7u5xsdejfe3Qp8A","clues":["utility_poles"],"important":false,"tagged":true},{"id":"rEQ4","text":["**BERHENTI** stop signs and **BERI LALUAN** yield signs are both unique to Malaysia."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Untitled_design__2824_29.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/qn48nvMwybn7vaQP6","clues":["signs"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"H5tX","text":["Malaysian bollards will often have the colours **black**, **white**, **grey** and **red**. Here are three examples of typical Malaysian bollards.","NOTE: There can be multiple varieties of these bollards, but the layout is mostly the same."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Untitled_design__2823_29.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/VF2uZG1qdY85Aw9Z9","clues":["bollards"],"important":false,"tagged":true},{"id":"LlHN","text":["This is a typical Malaysian directional sign. **Hexagonal yellow **highway shields** **are unique to Malaysia."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/directionalsign.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/CeJasroXurz5dwqC7","clues":["signs"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"TekU","text":["Malaysian kilometre markers have a unique **white-and-blue **colour scheme. Note that the hexagon shields are often visible."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Untitled_design__2830_29.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/w1fXrLcG2AfWexGX7","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"1Mkw","text":["The **Malay language** uses the Latin script. It is very closely related to Indonesian. These two languages are practically indistinguishable for people who do not speak either."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/my_language.webp","link":"","clues":["language"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"GMuK","text":["In contrast to neighbouring Indonesia, **Chinese characters** are often seen in Malaysia. In fact, 24.6% of the Malaysian population is of Chinese descent."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/chinese.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/1yL5UJiPS593xoNh9","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"X4Fj","text":["Signposts in Malaysia almost always have **black-and-white** **stripes**.","NOTE: Within Asia, these posts are also found in Sri Lanka, Bhutan, India, Nepal and Bangladesh. Make sure to check other clues before guessing."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/signpost.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/9jwtYKkzUYvhPbjN6","clues":["signs"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"GNKN","text":["**Black-and-white **curbs are commonly found in Malaysia.","NOTE: Many other countries in Asia can also have black-and-white curbs."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/kerb.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/w9fDK214KyxXFxMk9","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false}]},{"title":"Regional and state-specific clues","title_zh":"州別專屬線索","items":[{"id":"tGn7","text":["Each Malaysian state, excluding the three federal territories, has its own road numbering system with a **unique letter** at the start of the road number.","NOTE: Sabah also has A roads, but only the A2 and A7."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/my_roads.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/Ex61LZ4fv1TJtjvGA","clues":["road_numbering","language"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"3C19","text":["**State flags** can be seen with some regularity, so it is worth learning them."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/malaysia_state_flags.webp","link":"","clues":["flags"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"4IWF","text":["Malaysian postal codes are useful to know, since they can be found on most street signs in the country. "],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/malaysia_postal_codes_new.webp","link":"","clues":["signs"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"Fn5n","text":["**Black pole stickers** are most commonly found on the mainland.","NOTE: The black stickers on Borneo only exist in Generation 4 coverage."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/MalayBlackStickers.webp","link":"https://maps.app.goo.gl/8U23grG4MkMxmbEFA","clues":["utility_poles"],"important":false,"tagged":true},{"id":"DVpF","text":["Black stickers with the text ‘**TEL TNB**’ at the bottom, are only found in Johor."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/TEL_TNB_Johor_Black_Sticker.webp","link":"https://www.google.com/maps/@1.5189436,103.7986263,3a,21.7y,129.61h,79.69t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1s1XGZcblrLaXJUJG5qoZKNQ!2e0!7i13312!8i6656?entry=ttu","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"FqOz","text":["**White pole stickers** are only found on electricity poles on the island of Borneo, in Sarawak."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/White_Sticker.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/9UCQbRAuiaKvLAkW8","clues":["utility_poles"],"important":false,"tagged":true},{"id":"c4nQ","text":["Lamp posts with **two small circles** on the support are mainly found on mainland Malaysia."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/my_twocircleslamppost.webp","link":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?api=1&fov=17.531467769923246&heading=165.6592265935562&map_action=pano&pano=Dns61o4eRAsfO8ZdTue4rQ&pitch=23.827270433913796&viewpoint=1.53175%2C103.752783","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"PHYA","text":["Lamp posts with a **triangular metal support** are mainly found on mainland Malaysia."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Triangular_Metal_Mainland_Lamp_Post.webp","link":"https://www.google.com/maps/@2.7610997,102.237736,3a,19y,54.94h,131.15t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1sHN4aoVxo9PPndJk4b5QWIQ!2e0!7i13312!8i6656?entry=ttu","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"4IDp","text":["Electricity poles on the Borneo side typically have a **2-1 insulator configuration**, and a long **diagonal wooden support**. They are exclusive to the Sarawak region of the island.","NOTE: Indonesian poles can look similar, but they are usually not made of wood, and use smaller or no diagonal supports."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Diagonal_Support_Poles.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/ckyTS9EtUATDRKJr7","clues":["utility_poles"],"important":false,"tagged":true},{"id":"AlbW","text":["Thin metal poles with **two parallel **pole tops are exclusive to the Sabah region of Borneo."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Two_Horizontal_Support_Poles.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/yBUpZzPgr934PqJD7","clues":["utility_poles"],"important":false,"tagged":true},{"id":"VXzD","text":["This lamp post with a supporting piece of sheet metal resembling a **boomerang** is found in Sarawak.","NOTE: It is more common in cities other than Kuching."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Sarawak_Lamp_Posts.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/XEDwXRdrZESv1NNEA","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"VZEz","text":["Trash bins with a **logo resembling an ‘S’** are found in the states of Negeri Sembilan, Malacca and Johor."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/my_malaccabins.webp","link":"https://maps.app.goo.gl/y8TTpyS2oMP8Hy6h7","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"7iWU","text":["Trash bins with a **logo resembling leaves** are found in Perlis and Kedah."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/my_kedahbins.webp","link":"https://maps.app.goo.gl/6dEbR4DHXgYEepgq5","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"SLFX","text":["Trash bins with this logo featuring a **sunny landscape**, saying **‘Alam Flora’** are found in Pahang, Kuala Lumpur and Putrajaya. The logo will occasionally be absent, and it will just say ‘Alam Flora’."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/my_kualalumpurbins.webp","link":"https://maps.app.goo.gl/n3CSZfspZKFSEHpCA","clues":["scenery"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"lopw","text":["**Yellow street name signs** with a black outline are specific to the state of Johor.","NOTE: This **arrow-shaped** street sign, regardless of its colour, is exclusive to Malaysia.","NOTE: Yellow signs are also found in southern [Negeri Sembilan](https://maps.app.goo.gl/HG89SePzMd5WWheo6), however only the tip of the arrow will be black."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Johor_Street_Sign.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/VXzBV1PLXpR4YRVp9","clues":["street_names","signs"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"m7su","text":["**Green** street signs that form an arrow shape and have a **yellow hexagonal symbol **with the letters** JKR** on the left side are found in Sabah."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Sabah_Street_Signs.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/sPWtadXnL7eMFFwF6","clues":["language","signs"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"ZWP5","text":["Assuming you are on Borneo: the state of Sabah is **very mountainous**, and much of the coverage is on mountain roads like this one.","NOTE: Sarawak generally has flatter roads. Even if you see mountains, they will usually be at a [distance](https://goo.gl/maps/5VrnWWJCBfNgREaP7)."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Sabah_Mountains.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/z6PRqQJHLipvL9eu7","clues":["scenery"],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"vYmT","text":["These **isolated rock formations**, rising abruptly from an otherwise flat landscape, can be found near the Thai border in Perlis state."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Perlis_State_Isolated_Rock_Formations.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/mE7o9R7VqevTMvLd9","clues":["scenery"],"important":false,"tagged":false}]},{"title":"Spotlight","title_zh":"重點地標","items":[{"id":"4Be2","text":["Urban areas in Labuan are dotted with **blue cylindrical containers**."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Labuan_blue_bins.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/gM41nteDBtWu4c3H6","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false},{"id":"0dJK","text":["This unique **grey car** with a long front antenna can be found in Gunung Mulu National Park, Sarawak."],"text_zh":[],"image":"plonkit/malaysia/Sarawak_Gunung_Mulu_National_Park_Google_Car.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/6ZEMJFXZnpo9fB9i6","clues":[],"important":false,"tagged":false}]}],"tip_count":32,"facts":{"driving_side":"left","phone_numbers":"+60","domains":[".my"],"currencies":[{"name":"Malaysian ringgit","symbol":"RM","status":"official","code":"MYR"}],"years":["2013","2014","2015","2016","2017","2018","2019","2020","2021","2022","2024","2025","2026"],"lines":[["white"],["white"],["white"]]},"gallery":{"architecture":[{"image":"geohints/architecture/malaysia_1.webp","link":"https://goo.gl/maps/XeB